  "findings": [
    "Hosted GPU silently ignores level — and accepts \"BANANA\" with HTTP 200",
    "Compression cache is blind to kind/level, collapsing any per-segment policy",
    "Hosted endpoint does not validate API keys → silently unattributed usage",
    "Intent dominates compression, but stock passes one stale intent per request",
    "tag_messages/assign_level are dead code; hosted path sends kind: null",
    "Proxy hardcodes /v1, breaking Gemini/OpenRouter/Groq-style base URLs",
    "Documented tools/view_trace.py does not exist (we wrote one)",
    "shadow_storage: \"redis\" validates but is unimplemented → silent data loss",
    "The two kind classifiers disagree; the conversation-aware one mislabels every file read"
  ],
  "corrections": [
    {
      "was": "79% fewer tokens / 3.1× on a drift session",
      "why": "A hand-constructed example, not a benchmark result — the real agent sessions didn't reproduce it."
    },
    {
      "was": "1.61× rel/1k on the drift session",
      "why": "An artefact of a cache poisoned during a hosted-GPU outage: passthrough segments were cached as if compressed. Fixed and re-run to a clean pass."
    },
    {
      "was": "+9pp must-keep retention at N=3 — \"a modest but real win\"",
      "why": "Not fabricated or buggy, just didn't hold: +9.0pp → +6.8pp → +5.3pp → +3.8pp as campaigns grew from 3 to the full pre-registered 8, while task-relevant retention turned out slightly negative once all 8 were in."
    }
  ],
  "live_status_note": "The result above is offline-only. Live solve-rate A/B was attempted -- four separate recording attempts across two days -- and stopped: Gemini's free-tier quota killed every one before completion. The adaptive regret-loop controller is built and unit-tested but was never run live for the same reason. Both are labelled \"built, not proven\" in docs/results.md, not claimed as validated.",
  "verdict": "Intent/kind routing does not reliably beat Paritok's stock defaults. At the full pre-registered N=8 campaigns, kind_only equals stock exactly on every metric. Intent routing's must-keep effect shrank as N grew (+9.0pp at N=3 -> +3.8pp at N=8, 5 of 8 campaigns positive, 3 negative) and task-relevant retention -- the metric that matters most -- is slightly WORSE under routing (97% vs 99% for stock in the campaign population). Building on this evidence would not be justified."
}